---
// Fills the empty space every page has between the sticky nav and its own
// <h1> (the `pt-28 sm:pt-36` top padding every top-level page section
// uses) with an admin-managed image, when one's configured for that page
// (see /admin/site-properties, page_banners table). Renders nothing at all
// when no image is set — the section just stays plain black (the body's
// own bg-brand-ink), same as before this existed.
//
// Deliberately only covers the top band of the section (a fixed height,
// not the whole section) — most of these pages have a lot of content below
// the header, and this is meant to decorate the header gap, not become a
// full-page background image. The gradient fades the image out to solid
// ink by the bottom of that band so it blends into the rest of the (black)
// page rather than hard-cutting off.
//
// Usage: add `relative` to the page's <section> (needed so the two
// absolutely-positioned divs below anchor to it), then drop
// <PageBanner imageUrl={...} /> as the section's first child, before the
// <h1>.
//
// Deliberately NOT `overflow-hidden` on that section, even though it might
// look like the obvious pairing with `relative` here — both of this
// component's own divs are already self-bounding (`inset-x-0 top-0` plus an
// explicit `h-40`/`sm:h-56`, and a CSS `background-image` is clipped to its
// own box regardless of overflow), so overflow-hidden was never actually
// doing any clipping work for THIS component. What it does do is make that
// <section> a scroll container, which — per the exact same overflow-not-
// visible-creates-a-scroll-container rule documented at length in
// global.css next to `[data-sticky-thead]` — hijacks position:sticky for
// every frozen table header anywhere inside that section (or inside a
// fragment loaded into it), making them stick to the section instead of the
// page. That's exactly how standings/team-standings/roster/teams/driver
// profile/driver stats/team stats/hall of fame/awards all silently lost
// their sticky headers (Logan's report, Sept 2026) while results pages —
// the one place this component ISN'T used — kept working. Confirmed via the
// same Playwright rect-inspection technique used for the original
// overflow-x-auto version of this bug: adding overflow-hidden back
// reproduces it instantly, removing it fixes it instantly, and no visual
// difference appears either way (nothing here ever relied on it clipping
// anything). If a future page genuinely needs to clip something that
// bleeds past its own box, scope overflow-hidden to a wrapper around just
// that element instead of the whole section.
interface Props {
  imageUrl: string | null;
}

const { imageUrl } = Astro.props;
---

{imageUrl && (
  <>
    <div
      class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-0 -z-20 h-40 bg-cover bg-center sm:h-56"
      style={`background-image: url('${imageUrl}')`}
    >
    </div>
    <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-0 -z-10 h-40 bg-gradient-to-b from-brand-ink/30 via-brand-ink/80 to-brand-ink sm:h-56"></div>
  </>
)}
